# Copy to .env and edit literal values. Never commit .env.
# Apply edits during maintenance: ./start.sh (restarts services; retains saved data)
# Docker defaults come first. Native-only and advanced settings are optional.
# No shell ${...} expansion. Quote secrets containing # or spaces with single quotes.
# URL passwords must be percent-encoded; never put raw @, /, # or : in a URL password.
# Docker reads this file directly; no legacy model JSON or sibling .env is needed.
# See README: Docker quick start and configuration reference.
# Select CSV, knowledge source and target in the app; use bundled agent skills.
# Startup registers bundled HeartFailure and user-inputs/*/research.json automatically.
# Advanced input overrides are documented in README, not enabled by this template.

# Database identities, passwords, read-only accounts and Docker storage are automatic.
# Keep generated .memstara/ and compose.override.yaml with this installation.

# Select the dataset and target in the app: Data & target / research input editor.

# Host folder for generated files: prepared dataset subsets, saved model artifacts,
# evaluation results, reports and execution traces. Database records are stored separately.
# This does NOT select the original CSV, knowledge source or prediction target;
# choose those in the app's research input / Data & target settings.
# Default "outputs" means the outputs/ folder beside this project .env file.
# Docker mounts this host folder at /app/outputs; normally leave this value unchanged.
# Keep this folder to retain saved files. Changing the path does not move old results.
# After changing it, run ./start.sh during maintenance to apply the new mount.
MEMSTARA_OUTPUT_DIR=outputs

# Select the predictive model through the ML agent skills in the app.

MEMSTARA_LLM_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY

# Foundry: supply the resource NAME or MEMSTARA_LLM_API_BASE resource-root URL.
# If both are provided they must agree. API key is supplied by your resource owner.
MEMSTARA_LLM_RESOURCE=YOUR_RESOURCE_NAME

# The only published Docker port. Choose a free port on 127.0.0.1.
MEMSTARA_WEB_PORT=5173


# Required for execution: provider and actual deployment name.
MEMSTARA_LLM_PROVIDER=azure_foundry

MEMSTARA_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# Optional alternative to MEMSTARA_LLM_RESOURCE: unset the resource name first.
# MEMSTARA_LLM_API_BASE=https://YOUR_RESOURCE_NAME.services.ai.azure.com

# Optional numeric generation settings; temperature 0..2, max_tokens 1..200000.
# MEMSTARA_LLM_TEMPERATURE=1

# Model assignments belong in this .env; MEMSTARA_STAGE_MODELS_PATH is not supported.
# No sibling Motoro .env is loaded. PATH and ordinary OS settings remain inherited.
# Optional Question Universe local embeddings (viewer only, no remote inference).
# Rebuild the viewer API with this flag; cache the pinned model first.
MEMSTARA_UNIVERSE_SEMANTICS=0

# The full Docker stack uses HF_HOME for its embedding cache.

# No manual pricing configuration is required to install or run Memstara.
# Optional manual rates: app > Settings and more > Cost estimate settings.
# Rates are stored as generated application data under outputs/pricing/.
# These are estimates, never actual Azure billing. Advanced overrides are documented
# in deployment/README.md; do not enter a pricing JSON for the default workflow.

# Additional optional configuration.

# For anthropic/openai/openrouter, set provider/model and MEMSTARA_LLM_API_KEY.
# Leave MEMSTARA_LLM_RESOURCE unset outside Azure Foundry.

# Optional group overrides; blank/unset inherits the default model above.
# Non-explanation: Question, Hypothesis, Data, ML and Interpretation.
# MEMSTARA_NON_EXPLANATION_PROVIDER=

# MEMSTARA_NON_EXPLANATION_MODEL=

# MEMSTARA_NON_EXPLANATION_API_BASE=

# MEMSTARA_EXPLANATION_PROVIDER=

# MEMSTARA_EXPLANATION_MODEL=

# MEMSTARA_EXPLANATION_API_BASE=

# MEMSTARA_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=8192

# MEMSTARA_NON_EXPLANATION_TEMPERATURE=1

# MEMSTARA_NON_EXPLANATION_MAX_TOKENS=8192

# MEMSTARA_EXPLANATION_TEMPERATURE=1

# MEMSTARA_EXPLANATION_MAX_TOKENS=8192

# Optional effort: low, medium, high, xhigh or max; provider support varies.
# MEMSTARA_LLM_EFFORT=medium

# MEMSTARA_NON_EXPLANATION_EFFORT=medium

# MEMSTARA_EXPLANATION_EFFORT=medium

# Host model cache folder, relative to .env; full Docker stack mounts it at /app/cache.
HF_HOME=outputs/huggingface

# Conservative local compute limits (threads); tokenizer flag is true/false.
OMP_NUM_THREADS=1

OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1

MKL_NUM_THREADS=1

TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM=false

# Optional directory for shared Markdown instructions.
# MEMSTARA_SHARED_SKILLS_DIR=

# Optional directory for user-authored skills; bundled skills remain unchanged.
# MEMSTARA_USER_SKILLS_DIR=

# Optional JSON leakage-exclusion rules; see DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md.
# MEMSTARA_LEAKAGE_RULES_PATH=

# Optional JSON specialist source configuration; not an API credential.
# MEMSTARA_EXPLANATION_SOURCES_JSON='{}'
# Leave unset to use the selected OKF corpus.

# Host folder exposed read-only at /app/user-inputs in Docker. Put private CSV/OKF here.
MEMSTARA_INPUTS_DIR=./user-inputs

# Full Docker stack requires a unique project name. Use a new name for an independent install.
# Do not reuse an existing native provisioning project without an explicit data migration.
# Filesystem defaults in Docker: examples/... (bundled), user-inputs/... (host folder).
# The web port is published on 127.0.0.1 only; API/control/DB ports remain internal.
# Docker service credentials come from the DSNs above; no separate password variables.

# Native-only settings: not needed by ./start.sh or the root compose.yml.
# Native API/control listeners default to these ports. Docker uses internal
# API 8000 and control 8072 regardless of these overrides.
# MEMSTARA_API_PORT=8071
# MEMSTARA_CONTROL_PORT=8072

# Only viewer/docker-compose.yml reads this legacy viewer cache setting.
# For the full Docker stack use HF_HOME above instead.
# MEMSTARA_EMBEDDING_CACHE=../outputs/embedding-cache
